🔥 Redis vs Snowflake — side by side

         REDIS APPROACH                    SNOWFLAKE APPROACH
              Redis                              No Redis
                |                                  |
       ┌────────┼────────┐                ┌────────┼────────┐
       ↓        ↓        ↓                ↓        ↓        ↓
      S1       S2       S3               S1       S2       S3
       |        |        |                |        |        |
       └───────→Redis←───┘                Generate locally
                |                                  |
             1001,1002,1003                 Timestamp
                                                   +
                                              Worker ID
                                                   +
                                              Sequence
                                                   |
                                                   ↓
                                             Unique ID

The simplest way to remember:

Redis:

“Central counter, give me the next number.”

Snowflake:

“Every server has enough information to create its own unique number.”

And then both approaches can feed that number into Base62:

Unique ID
   ↓
Base62
   ↓
7-character short code
   ↓
Database

For a high-scale URL shortener, I’d generally prefer Snowflake-style ID generation because the ID generation doesn’t require a network call to Redis on every URL creation.